{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED — independent review of the composite-kinds design note at exact head a63f0953c2f52e965406c5cbd682cee17a365c8c, artifact cf4739f2 at notes/2026-08-20-composite-kinds.md, for request 2daf1efd.\n\nCONDITION 1, kind-defs sound. Verified against the code at this head. validateDefinition (internal/workroom/kinds.go:366, :376) closes both sets — render to the seven classes, lifecycle to none/request/promise/report — so the note is right that undertake's proposed lifecycle \"undertaking\" needs an evaluator release, and right that submit's render:artifact plus lifecycle:none are already inside the closed sets and need none. promise does declare countKinds(1,1,KindRequest) at kinds.go:168, matching \"basis: count(1..1, request)\", and the fold does separately re-read bases through basesOfLifecycle, exactly as the note describes. undertake's four checks and submit's three are each total and typed as written. The basis-constraint change reads consistently across the undertake definition, its check 4, and the basis-constraint section.\n\nCONDITION 2, three preservation claims hold. Promise-before-report: submit's 1..1 claim basis plus the total author check leaves no path to a completion without a prior claim by the same actor. Exact-head approval invalidation: the head lives in body.commit, and both validateReview and reviewedPaths read the body, so fusing the pointer into the report cannot weaken a check that reads the pointer. Reviewer's claim act: correctly kept, and the note's justification is measured, not asserted — at depth 7235 the log holds exactly 23 records refused \"report has no promise\", which I counted at 23 both at and below that depth and still 23 now.\n\nCONDITION 3, citations. Exactly fifteen event ids: eleven written prefix-to-suffix each resolve to exactly one record, and 40f8bfd0, a84b6441, bac269be, fcd6a4be each resolve to exactly one. All three cited commits exist — ca2836ab, fc63ec40, 8b427acf. Artifact bac269be doe